  ⚠ Start a git repository in /srv/files-example and take it over?                                                      
                                                                                                                        
  Yes looks at the folder once more and makes the changes listed below only if its list is unchanged. The folder belongs
  to the engine rootless:alice. Containers of these stacks already run, so deploying would create duplicate containers  
  and take their ports twice. qhost only warns.                                                                         
                                                                                                                        
    folder: /srv/files-example                                                                                          
    case: files (files without a repository; a first commit takes the listed files)                                     
    engine: rootless:alice                                                                                              
    owner: root, group: root, mode: 0755                                                                                
    the service can write it: no                                                                                        
    permissions are set: yes                                                                                            
                                                                                                                        
  Files of the first commit (2)                                                                                         
    demo/.env                                                                                                           
    demo/compose.yaml                                                                                                   
                                                                                                                        
  Left out (2), not needed by the stacks, kept out of git by .gitignore                                                 
    demo/data: bind-mount (stack demo)                                                                                  
    demo/notes.txt: not-referenced                                                                                      
                                                                                                                        
  Stacks (1)                                                                                                            
    demo (folder demo)                                                                                                  
      works: deploy                                                                                                     
      does not work: backup                                                                                             
      warning secrets-env-not-ignored: secrets.env is not listed in .gitignore                                          
      not resolvable: env_file "${CONF_DIR}/app.env": variable CONF_DIR has no value in .env                            
      conflict: the container demo-app-1 of the project old-demo runs in the folder, in the engine system               
                                                                                                                        
  Changes after yes                                                                                                     
    A git repository is started with branch main and a first commit of the listed files as qhost. It is taken over as a 
    local stack folder.                                                                                                 
    A .gitignore is created with the 2 paths left out in a block marked by qhost, and the first commit holds it. No     
    other file in the folder is written.                                                                                
    3 paths get the group of the service account with group write; the owner stays                                      
    The folder is added to the systemd drop-in of the service, which restarts once.                                     
